    "EBIT is modeled as GAAP consolidated operating income/(loss) from Ford\u2019s consolidated income statement; 2025 EBIT is negative (-$9.169B), consistent with the filed statement.",
    "D&A used for historical is computed as (depreciation and tooling amortization + other amortization) from the consolidated cash flow reconciliation. Because 'other amortization' is presented net in the cash-flow bridge, the combined D&A can differ from a simple gross depreciation/ammortization expense view.",
    "Capex is modeled from consolidated 'Capital spending' on the cash flow statement, converted to a positive absolute outflow amount (e.g., $8.236B for 2023).",
    "NWC is constructed from consolidated balance-sheet 'Total current assets' and 'Total current liabilities' using the formula: NWC = (Current assets - Cash and cash equivalents - Marketable securities) - (Current liabilities - Debt payable within one year). Restricted cash is excluded from NWC and instead carried via the separate cash input.",
